{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>O earth, cover not my blood</b> — as in (Job 31:37), 'If I have seen injustice in my heart, let not HaShem hear' — but Elohim did hear; and likewise: 'and my prayer is pure,' and <b>and earth</b> — if I have lied — <b>cover not my blood</b>." "<b>And let there be no place for my cry</b> — my cry finds no place." "And some say: <b>O earth</b> — reveal my violence; and let there be no place where my cry lingers, but let it rise at once."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The quoted parallel is from Job 31:37; Ibn Ezra's syntax is compressed, chaining several scriptural echoes together."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:51.596419346Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}